# somethingThatNoTableLists(Buffer.from("abc"))[keyThatNoTableLists]   The program names neither Buffer.prototype.parent nor process.send (runtimefunction 65568; 65561 is called on behalf of process.send).
# Reading an accessor is calling its getter. The receiver may be the buffer and the key may be "parent", so the function of the library behind the accessor is in the program and the read is not refused.
# A function that the program would have to call stays out: the call throws the error that names it.
